 * @brief Retrieves the current state of the Software Power Manager (SPM) module.
 *
 * This function simply reads the value of the `SpmCtrl_Status` global variable and returns it.
 * The returned value represents the current operational state of the SPM, which can be:
 *
 * - `Spm_Initialized`: The module is initialized but not yet running.
 * - `Spm_Running`: The module is running and handling power profile requests.
